    "figures": [
        {
            "claim_index": 19,
            "claim": "1. Figure 1: Overview of Anisotropic Spectral Error Dressing (ASED). Given a deterministic GraphCast forecast, ASED: (1) computes spherical harmonic coefficients of historical residuals, (2) estimates degree spectrum Cl and within-degree anisotropy weights wµ across 3 µ-bins and 4 degree bands, (3) generates M = 50 ensemble members by sampling Gaussian perturbations with the calibrated anisotropic spectral structure.",
            "verdict": "Verified",
            "explanation": "Analysis stage: The pipeline parameters cited in Figure 1 (M=50, 3 µ-bins, 4 degree bands) are confirmed by optimize_trace/iteration_0/RESULTS.json which records: ensemble_size=50, n_mu_bins=3, n_aniso_bands=4. The three-step pipeline matches ased.py's implementation. The methodology steps match the code in sht_utils.py (SHT coefficients), ased.py (anisotropy weight estimation), and the ASED sampler (ensemble generation). The figure is an overview diagram whose claimed parameters are verified by the result artifact.",
            "evidence": "exp/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS/optimize_trace/iteration_0/RESULTS.json; exp/ased/perturbations/ased.py; exp/ased/spectral/sht_utils.py; exp/ased/scripts/run_ased_optimized.py",
            "detection_mode": "static_code_analysis",
            "decision_stage": "analysis",
            "analysis_classification": {
                "bucket": "static_verifiable"
            },
            "verification_process": {
                "files_analyzed": [
                    "exp/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS/optimize_trace/iteration_0/RESULTS.json",
                    "exp/ased/perturbations/ased.py",
                    "exp/ased/spectral/sht_utils.py",
                    "exp/ased/scripts/run_ased_optimized.py"
                ],
                "commands_executed": []
            }
        },
        {
            "claim_index": 20,
            "claim": "2. Figure 2: Scale-dependent anisotropy in GraphCast Z500 forecast errors. Each bar group shows the relative power in 3 µ-bins (zonal: µ < 0.33, intermediate: 0.33 ≤ µ < 0.67, meridional: µ ≥ 0.67) for 4 degree bands. Synoptic scales (l = 24–59) show the strongest anisotropy with zonal/meridional ratio of 5.99. Dashed line indicates isotropic reference (33.3 %).",
            "verdict": "Verified",
            "explanation": "Analysis stage: The anisotropy ratios underlying Figure 2 are confirmed by optimize_trace/iteration_0/RESULTS.json: Band 2 (l=24-59) has ratio_first_over_last: 5.994541... ≈ 5.99. All four bands' weights are recorded in the JSON artifact. The 3-bin boundaries (0.33, 0.67) match the n_mu_bins=3 with uniform binning in ased.py. The dashed isotropic reference (33.3%) is consistent with 1/3 power per bin for 3 equal bins.",
